['```javascript
// Define a class to manage script rendering with caching and concurrency control
class ScriptRenderer {
  constructor() {
    this.cache = new Map();
    this.scriptQueue = [];
    this.loadingScripts = 0;
    this.maxLoadingScripts = 5;
  }

  // Function to validate script objects
  isValidScript(script) {
    return script.type && typeof script.code === 'string' && script.code.trim().length > 0;
  }

  // Function to fetch and cache scripts from an external API
  async fetchScript(url) {
    if (this.cache.has(url)) {
      return this.cache.get(url);
    }
    try {
      const response = await fetch(url);
      if (!response.ok) {
        throw new Error('Network response was not ok');
      }
      const scriptCode = await response.text();
      this.cache.set(url, scriptCode);
      return scriptCode;
    } catch (error) {
      console.error(`Failed to fetch script from ${url}:`, error);
      return null;
    }
  }

  // Function to render scripts in the footer
  async renderScript(script) {
    if (!this.isValidScript(script)) {
      console.error('Invalid script object:', script);
      return '';
    }
    const scriptCode = script.type.includes('text/javascript') ? script.code : await this.fetchScript(script.src);
    if (scriptCode) {
      const scriptTag = document.createElement('script');
      scriptTag.type = 'text/javascript';
      scriptTag.text = scriptCode;
      document.body.appendChild(scriptTag);
      return `<script type="text/javascript">${scriptCode}</script>`;
    }
    return '';
  }

  // Function to limit concurrent script creation
  async processScriptQueue() {
    while (this.scriptQueue.length > 0 && this.loadingScripts < this.maxLoadingScripts) {
      const script = this.scriptQueue.shift();
      if (await this.renderScript(script)) {
        this.loadingScripts--;
      }
    }
  }

  // Function to add scripts to the queue and process them
  async addScriptToFooter(script) {
    if (!this.scriptQueue.includes(script)) {
      this.scriptQueue.push(script);
    }
    this.loadingScripts++;
    await this.processScriptQueue();
  }

  // Function to render all scripts in the footer
  async renderFooterScripts(scripts) {
    const renderedScripts = await Promise.all(scripts.map(script => this.addScriptToFooter(script)));
    return `<footer>${renderedScripts.join('')}</footer>`;
  }
}

// Example usage
const renderer = new ScriptRenderer();
const scripts = [
  { type: 'text/javascript', code: 'console.log("Hello, world!");' },
  { src: 'https://example.com/script.js' }
];
renderer.renderFooterScripts(scripts).then(html => console.log(html));
```

This code snippet provides a basic implementation of the `ScriptRenderer` class, which encapsulates the functionality required to dynamically render scripts in the footer of a web page. It includes caching for external API fetches, concurrency control to limit the number of scripts being loaded simultaneously, and validation for script objects. The `renderFooterScripts` method returns a promise that resolves to the minified HTML string representing the footer with all necessary scripts rendered.']

